```java
class HelloWorld {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("My first Java program!");
    }
}
```
Explanation of components:
-   `class HelloWorld`: Defines a class named `HelloWorld`. In Java, all code resides within classes.
-   `public static void main(String[] args)`: This is the main method, the entry point of the program execution.
    -   `public`: Access modifier, making the method visible to the Java Virtual Machine (JVM).
    -   `static`: Allows the method to be called without creating an object of the class.
    -   `void`: Indicates that the method does not return any value.
    -   `String[] args`: An array to hold command-line arguments.
-   `System.out.println("My first Java program!");`: This statement prints the string "My first Java program!" to the console, followed by a new line. `System.out` is an object representing the standard output stream, and `println()` is a method to print text.
